problem:
Problem description
- There is a directed communication network with node set $$\mathcal{N}$$, source node $$s \in \mathcal{N}$$, sink node $$t \in \mathcal{N}$$, and a mandatory service node $$m \in \mathcal{N}$$.
- The network data are given by a bandwidth-capacity matrix $$B=[b_{ij}]$$ over node pairs $$i,j \in \mathcal{N}$$, where $$b_{ij} \ge 0$$ is the available direct bandwidth from $$i$$ to $$j$$.
- A zero entry in $$B$$ means that no direct link is available between the corresponding nodes.
- The planning horizon is static and is represented by $$\mathcal{T}$$ as a single planning stage.
- The goal is to choose a route from $$s$$ to $$t$$ that must pass through $$m$$ and maximize the route bandwidth, where the route bandwidth is the smallest bandwidth among the selected direct links on that route.
- The selected route must be loop-free, meaning no node may be visited more than once.
- Only available direct links with positive bandwidth may be used.
- If several feasible routes achieve the same maximum bandwidth, any one of them is acceptable.
- No demand data are present in this problem.
- No separate cost objective is active in this problem; if a generic implementation needs one, it may be denoted by a link-cost matrix $$C=[c_{ij}]$$, though it is not used here.
- A solution is represented by:
  - an ordered simple path $$\pi=(v_0,v_1,\ldots,v_L)$$ with $$v_0=s$$ and $$v_L=t$$, and with $$m$$ appearing somewhere along the path;
  - a binary link-selection pattern $$x_{ij}$$ indicating whether direct link $$\left(i,j\right)$$ is used;
  - a scalar bottleneck bandwidth $$z$$ giving the minimum selected link bandwidth along the chosen route.

Input Format
{
  "sets": {
    "nodes": {
      "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{N}$$",
      "indexing": "$$i,j \\in \\mathcal{N}$$"
    },
    "time_horizon": {
      "symbol": "$$\\mathcal{T}$$",
      "meaning": "static single-stage planning set"
    }
  },
  "parameters": {
    "source_node": {
      "symbol": "$$s$$",
      "type": "node label"
    },
    "sink_node": {
      "symbol": "$$t$$",
      "type": "node label"
    },
    "mandatory_service_node": {
      "symbol": "$$m$$",
      "type": "node label"
    },
    "capacity_matrix": {
      "symbol": "$$B=[b_{ij}]$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{N}| \\times |\\mathcal{N}|$$",
      "meaning": "direct bandwidth capacity for each ordered node pair; $$b_{ij}=0$$ means no direct link"
    },
    "cost_matrix_optional": {
      "symbol": "$$C=[c_{ij}]$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{N}| \\times |\\mathcal{N}|$$",
      "meaning": "optional generic link-cost data, not used in the stated objective"
    }
  },
  "planning_goal": {
    "symbol": "$$z$$",
    "meaning": "maximize the bottleneck bandwidth of a simple route from $$s$$ to $$t$$ that passes through $$m$$"
  }
}

Output Format
{
  "route": {
    "path": {
      "symbol": "$$\\pi=(v_0,v_1,\\ldots,v_L)$$",
      "meaning": "ordered node sequence of the selected simple route from $$s$$ to $$t$$ that includes $$m$$"
    },
    "selected_links": {
      "symbol": "$$X=[x_{ij}]$$",
      "shape": "$$|\\mathcal{N}| \\times |\\mathcal{N}|$$",
      "meaning": "binary description of which direct links are used in the route"
    }
  },
  "bandwidth": {
    "symbol": "$$z$$",
    "meaning": "maximum achievable bottleneck bandwidth of the chosen route"
  }
}

Example(s)

Input 1
{
  "sets": {
    "nodes": ["$$A$$", "$$B$$", "$$C$$", "$$D$$", "$$E$$"],
    "time_horizon": "$$\\mathcal{T}$$"
  },
  "parameters": {
    "source_node": "$$A$$",
    "sink_node": "$$E$$",
    "mandatory_service_node": "$$C$$",
    "capacity_matrix": [
      ["$$0$$", "$$90$$", "$$85$$", "$$0$$", "$$65$$"],
      ["$$95$$", "$$0$$", "$$70$$", "$$65$$", "$$34$$"],
      ["$$60$$", "$$0$$", "$$0$$", "$$88$$", "$$80$$"],
      ["$$67$$", "$$30$$", "$$25$$", "$$0$$", "$$84$$"],
      ["$$0$$", "$$51$$", "$$0$$", "$$56$$", "$$0$$"]
    ]
  }
}
